license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
url: https://geo-sciml.com
repository-code: https://github.com/pankajkmishra/geo-sciml
abstract: >-
  This book introduces geoscientific machine learning with Julia, combining
  practical coding workflows with scientific reasoning for Earth-system problems.
  It develops core machine-learning concepts, then advances to physics-informed
  and operator-learning methods used in scientific machine learning. The emphasis
  is on reproducible, computation-ready examples and on connecting data-driven
  models to governing physics, inverse problems, and geoscience applications.
keywords:
  - geoscience
  - machine learning
  - scientific machine learning
  - Julia
  - geophysics
  - inverse problems
